.Dd @MDOCDATE@
.Dt CLOWN-AGENT-SCOPE 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm clown-agent-scope
.Nd what a confined clown session's unit is: home, network, binds, environment, proxies, bridge
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A confined clown session runs its provider (claude) in an
.Em agent unit :
a transient systemd user service started by
.Nm clown
(FDR 0020, clown#244).
The frontend, the clown that holds the terminal, stays outside it and relays the
terminal.
This page says what the unit has, what it does not, and which sentences are
seen on a real host and which are read from the code.
The code is
.Pa internal/*/agentscope/unit.go ,
function
.Fn properties ;
a test (TestPropertyNamesAreTheDocumentedSet) fails when a property is added
or removed without this page's list below changing with it.
.Pp
Markers: (code) read from the source; (seen) observed on flic (NixOS, systemd
user manager) by the named recipe; (not tried) neither.
.Sh WHAT THE UNIT HAS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy Home
.Ev HOME
is
.Pa <worktree>/.tmp/agent-home ,
inside the worktree (code).
The operator's home and
.Pa /run/user
are an empty tmpfs (ProtectHome=tmpfs) holding only what is bound in (code).
.It Sy Claude config
.Ev CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
is a per-session directory in that home; the operator's
.Pa ~/.claude*
is not mounted (code).
With the model injection proxy the unit's credentials file is empty and the
environment holds only a placeholder; claude answered a one-line prompt in
such a unit (seen: explore-model-live-run, 2026-11-25).
.It Sy Network
None: PrivateNetwork=yes (code), so the host's loopback services and abstract
sockets are unreachable.
The only ways out are unix sockets bound in and relayed to loopback ports by
.Nm clown agent-exec :
the egress proxy (an HTTP CONNECT proxy with a host:port allow-list), forwarded
frontend servers, the statsd relay, the model injection proxy, the serve and
broker sockets, and the dead-man socket (code).
.It Sy Processes
A private pid namespace (PrivatePIDs=yes); the shim is the unit's init and
reaps what is reparented to it (code).
.It Sy cgroups
Every process of the unit, including a setsid child, is in the unit's own
cgroup; the tree has no sub-cgroup; creating one fails with a read-only file
system error (seen: explore-unit-cgroup-probe).
cgroupfs is read-only in the unit (ProtectControlGroups=yes, code).
.It Sy The user manager
Not reachable: no
.Pa /run/user/<uid>/systemd ,
an empty bus address, and
.Dq systemctl --user
fails to connect (seen: explore-unit-cgroup-probe).
.It Sy Files
Read-only view of the rest of the filesystem (ProtectSystem=strict), including
.Pa /etc
as the host has it (code); writable: the worktree, the spec's
.Em binds_rw ,
the single-inode sockets, and clown's plumbing paths (claude's projects
directory, hook state, moxy's log).
No bind may cover the launch directories (Spec.Validate).
.It Sy Environment
Built from an allow-list of the frontend's variables plus the spec's; the
user manager's own variables are unset (code, FDR 0020 "Environment").
.El
.Sh PROPERTIES
The properties of
.Fn properties
(the list the test pins; values in the source):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
PrivateUsers  PrivatePIDs  ProtectHome  TemporaryFileSystem
PrivateTmp  ProtectSystem  NoNewPrivileges  ProtectControlGroups
WorkingDirectory  PrivateNetwork  BindPaths  ReadWritePaths
BindReadOnlyPaths  InaccessiblePaths  MemoryHigh  MemoryMax
MemorySwapMax  TasksMax  CPUQuota  IOWeight  OOMPolicy  Restart
RuntimeMaxSec (unattended launches only)
.Ed
.Sh WHAT A WORKER CAN DO IN THE UNIT TODAY
Seen on flic, 2026-11-25 (explore-full-unit-probe, one run each):
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Dq nix build
of a tiny derivation works, and
.Dq nix develop
on a throwaway flake works.
.It
The nix daemon is reachable without being bound in (ProtectSystem=strict leaves
.Pa /nix/var
visible, and the unit keeps the operator's uid), and the unit is a
.Em trusted
user of it: the unit's
.Dq nix store info
says
.Dq Trusted: 1 .
A confined unit is therefore not a boundary for nix.
This is the operator's stopgap ruling, recorded here as seen, not changed.
.It
.Dq git ls-remote
and
.Dq git fetch
over HTTPS through the egress proxy work with no credential.
.Dq git push --dry-run
fails with no credential (no token file, no agent socket, no
.Pa ~/.ssh
in the agent home).
A real push and ssh were not tried.
.It
The unit cannot reach the operator's MCP servers, hooks or CLAUDE.md: it has no
access to the operator's claude config.
Servers clown starts for it are delivered as plugin servers.
.El
.Sh THE BRIDGE (FDR 0048)
There is one switch: the spec's
.Sy bridge
field, which spinclass writes from a trusted sweatfile knob.
Empty or absent is off: nothing is created and the serve is told so (its three
variables below are set empty).
.Sy offered
is on, and the launch goes on without a bridge if one cannot be set up (the
reason is in the result and on stderr).
.Sy required
is on, and a launch whose bridge cannot be set up is refused with the same
reason: before the unit starts when the cause is known then (no socket in 10 s,
a writable mount over the bridge directory or its cgroup file, routing refused,
no serve to route to), and by killing the unit when its cgroup cannot be
recorded.
Nothing in an environment turns the bridge on.
The session must be confined.
.Pp
The order, which both repositories keep:
clown prepares the launch directory and starts the serve with the three
variables; the serve binds the socket at once; clown waits up to 10 s for it,
then starts the unit; clown writes
.Pa bridge.cgroup
when systemd shows the unit's main process settled, before the provider;
.Nm bridge-listen
opens
.Em control
(admitted on identity alone: same user, the cgroup file, strict equality), says
ready, and only then does the provider start; clown writes the result (the
unit record) once the provider has started; the spawn's hello makes the
principal mapping, and only then are the verbs ready.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev CLOWN_BRIDGE_DIR , CLOWN_BRIDGE_UNIT , CLOWN_BRIDGE_CGROUP_FILE
Set by clown on spinclass's serve only (set empty when the bridge is off);
never passed into a unit.
.It Pa <runtime>/clown/launch/<key>/bridge/
The bridge directory, bound into the unit read-only at its own path; the serve
creates
.Pa bridge.sock
in it.
.It Pa <runtime>/clown/launch/<key>/bridge.cgroup
The unit's exact cgroup path, written by clown when systemd reports the unit
active (before the provider starts), mode 0600; not bound into the unit.
The serve admits a peer only if its cgroup equals this value
.Pq Fn CheckPeerExact .
The guarantee depends on the unit not being able to move processes between
cgroups (read-only cgroupfs) and not reaching the user manager (both above).
.It Ev CLOWN_BRIDGE_SOCKET
Set in the unit only, naming the socket.
.It Nm clown bridge-stdio , Nm clown bridge-listen
The inside half.
.Nm bridge-listen
holds the
.Em control
stream (retried for 15 s) and answers every endpoint with the fixed
.Dq the bridge is down
text once it ends.
.It Sy bridge-v1
Reported in the result's capabilities only after the cgroup file was written.
.It The result's Sy bridge No field
Absent when the spec did not ask for a bridge;
.Sy recorded
when the directory is bound and the unit's cgroup was written for the serve;
.Sy off: <reason>
when it was asked for and is missing.
.Sy recorded
is all the launch can know: the result is written once, at provider start, and
cannot see whether the listener admits the unit or whether
.Em control
opens.
That live state is the serve's: spinclass's state file, its counters and its
wake.
.El
.Sh KNOWN LIMITS
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Pa /etc
is the host's, read-only, including
.Pa /etc/claude-code ;
a trimmed per-unit
.Pa /etc
is ruled but not built.
.It
A process of the same account outside the unit can write
.Pa bridge.cgroup
and can move itself into any cgroup; cgroup identity means nothing against it.
.It
The operator's uid is the unit's uid (no dynamic user).
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clown 1 ,
.Xr clown-restart 1 ,
.Xr clown-stdio-bridge 1 ,
.Xr clownfile 5
.Pp
FDR 0020 (docs/features/0020-agent-scope-confinement.md) and FDR 0048 (circus
docs/features/0048-the-bridge.md) are the design records; this page is the
reference.
